  "body": "Following the [unstable](https://matrix.org/docs/spec/server_server/unstable.html#rules)/[HEAD](https://matrix.org/speculator/spec/HEAD/server_server/unstable.html#rules) spec, the `m.room.create` event must have `depth` set to `0`.\r\nLooking at events generated by synapse v0.24. when creating a room, `depth` is `1`.\r\nLooking at old rooms, like Matrix HQ, `depth` is `0`.\r\n\r\nIf the spec was adapted to either value, rooms that are created with the other values would all be invalid.\r\nSeems like the responsible changes where made in 2014 (thanks jzk for the links):\r\n- https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/commit/018443cb5914f8c4a5488397cc1c19689e949aff\r\n- https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/commit/e8323b9e344a557452b17f4e0dea9d95feff747f\r\n\r\nCode has moved since then: https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/commit/30057b1e154a0fdf1f778aa952c2f7c88656004e (thanks Magnap for the link)\r\n\r\nAccepting both depth values for the create event is not possible either, as it would open attack and room hijacking possibilities potentially, assuming that's the reason it was specifically set to a certain value in the spec?",
